<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. du Pré comes on the day of her second 300 mg dose of ocrelizumab. The three days of intravenous methylprednisolone a month ago caused a few nights of poor sleep and a metallic taste, and within two weeks the feeling in her fingers began to come back. The first infusion two weeks ago caused an itchy throat and flushing an hour in, which settled when the rate was slowed. She has worked with the occupational therapist on finger exercises and practices in 20-minute blocks, about two hours a day, and has played through slow movements without losing her place. The electric feeling on bending her head is fainter. Her blood tests before the first infusion were normal. She is less tired. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Treatment</td><td>Methylprednisolone 1 g for 3 days; ocrelizumab 300 mg two weeks ago; second 300 mg today</td></tr><tr><td>Infusion reaction</td><td>Mild throat itch and flushing with the first dose, settled by slowing the rate</td></tr><tr><td>Hand function</td><td>Feeling returning; practicing two hours a day in short blocks</td></tr><tr><td>Vaccination</td><td>Hepatitis B dose 2 today</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

